{"time": "2026-10-31T21:10:54+00:00", "call": 1, "arm": "B", "run": 1, "model": "gpt-oss-120b", "provider": "fake", "fingerprint": "fake", "tokens": {"prompt": 76, "completion": 434, "reasoning": 0}, "latency_s": 0.0, "reasoning_effort_dropped": false, "prompt": "Write a Python function optimize(func, dim, bounds, budget) that minimises a black-box function using at most `budget` calls to func, and returns (best_x, best_f, history). Use only numpy, math and random. Start your reply with a line '# Name: <short name>' and give the full code in one ```python block.", "raw": "# Name: PSOBaseline\n```python\n\"\"\"Standard global-best Particle Swarm Optimization (baseline).\n\nInertia-weight PSO with the constriction-equivalent parameters of Clerc &\nKennedy (2002): w = 0.7298, c1 = c2 = 1.49618. Velocities are clamped to a\nfraction of the search range; particles that leave the box are put back on the\nboundary and that velocity component is zeroed.\n\"\"\"\nimport numpy as np\n\n\ndef optimize(func, dim, bounds, budget, *, swarm_size=40, w=0.7298, c1=1.49618, c2=1.49618, vmax_frac=0.2):\n    lower, upper = (np.asarray(b, dtype=float) for b in bounds)\n    span = upper - lower\n    vmax = vmax_frac * span\n    n = min(swarm_size, budget)\n\n    x = lower + np.random.rand(n, dim) * span\n    v = np.random.uniform(-vmax, vmax, (n, dim))\n    f = np.empty(n)\n    history = []\n    gbest_f, gbest_x = np.inf, None\n    for i in range(n):\n        f[i] = func(x[i])\n        if f[i] < gbest_f:\n            gbest_f, gbest_x = f[i], x[i].copy()\n        history.append(gbest_f)\n    pbest_x, pbest_f = x.copy(), f.copy()\n    evals = n\n\n    while evals < budget:\n        r1, r2 = np.random.rand(n, dim), np.random.rand(n, dim)\n        v = w * v + c1 * r1 * (pbest_x - x) + c2 * r2 * (gbest_x - x)\n        v = np.clip(v, -vmax, vmax)\n        x = x + v\n        outside = (x < lower) | (x > upper)\n        x = np.clip(x, lower, upper)\n        v[outside] = 0.0\n\n        for i in range(n):\n            if evals >= budget:\n                break\n            fi = func(x[i])\n            evals += 1\n            if fi < pbest_f[i]:\n                pbest_f[i], pbest_x[i] = fi, x[i]\n                if fi < gbest_f:\n                    gbest_f, gbest_x = fi, x[i].copy()\n            history.append(gbest_f)\n\n    return gbest_x, gbest_f, history\n\n```\n", "name": "PSOBaseline", "code": "\"\"\"Standard global-best Particle Swarm Optimization (baseline).\n\nInertia-weight PSO with the constriction-equivalent parameters of Clerc &\nKennedy (2002): w = 0.7298, c1 = c2 = 1.49618. Velocities are clamped to a\nfraction of the search range; particles that leave the box are put back on the\nboundary and that velocity component is zeroed.\n\"\"\"\nimport numpy as np\n\n\ndef optimize(func, dim, bounds, budget, *, swarm_size=40, w=0.7298, c1=1.49618, c2=1.49618, vmax_frac=0.2):\n    lower, upper = (np.asarray(b, dtype=float) for b in bounds)\n    span = upper - lower\n    vmax = vmax_frac * span\n    n = min(swarm_size, budget)\n\n    x = lower + np.random.rand(n, dim) * span\n    v = np.random.uniform(-vmax, vmax, (n, dim))\n    f = np.empty(n)\n    history = []\n    gbest_f, gbest_x = np.inf, None\n    for i in range(n):\n        f[i] = func(x[i])\n        if f[i] < gbest_f:\n            gbest_f, gbest_x = f[i], x[i].copy()\n        history.append(gbest_f)\n    pbest_x, pbest_f = x.copy(), f.copy()\n    evals = n\n\n    while evals < budget:\n        r1, r2 = np.random.rand(n, dim), np.random.rand(n, dim)\n        v = w * v + c1 * r1 * (pbest_x - x) + c2 * r2 * (gbest_x - x)\n        v = np.clip(v, -vmax, vmax)\n        x = x + v\n        outside = (x < lower) | (x > upper)\n        x = np.clip(x, lower, upper)\n        v[outside] = 0.0\n\n        for i in range(n):\n            if evals >= budget:\n                break\n            fi = func(x[i])\n            evals += 1\n            if fi < pbest_f[i]:\n                pbest_f[i], pbest_x[i] = fi, x[